                <pb facs="0670" n="558" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg558"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 3892/2.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Snyder to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Jamaica</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-16"><hi rendition="#italic">January 16,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Fearful earthquake followed by fire; Kingston destroyed; hundreds of lives lost;
                    food sadly wanted. Consulate partially destroyed; fireproof safe.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
